    "confidence": "moderate",
    "plain": "Lifting the faith school admissions cap is likely to increase religious and ethnic segregation, which research links to weaker community cohesion \u2014 though the government argues the existing cap has not meaningfully improved diversity. The actual effect depends heavily on how many new schools open and where.",
    "biggest_unknown": "How many new 100%-faith-selective schools actually open and in which areas \u2014 if uptake is limited, the segregation effect is small; if the Catholic Church expands substantially, the effect could be larger.",
    "claims": [
      {
        "tier": "stated",
        "claim": "The policy lifts the cap on faith schools, allowing them to offer more places selected by faith and encouraging expansion.",
        "evidence_id": "M",
        "quote": "lift the cap on faith schools, allowing them to offer more places to children based on faith and encouraging their expansion"
      },
      {
        "tier": "projected",
        "claim": "Humanists UK research suggests that 100% religious selection drives racial segregation, with such schools being less ethnically diverse than those with the 50% cap.",
        "evidence_id": "E17",
        "quote": "Research from Humanists UK suggests that schools with a 50% cap are more ethnically diverse than those that select 100% of their pupils by religion, and that 100% religious selection drives racial segregation"
      },
      {
        "tier": "projected",
        "claim": "The Education Policy Institute concluded in 2017 that this policy is unlikely to increase social mobility and risks increased social segregation.",
        "evidence_id": "E18",
        "quote": "such a policy is \"unlikely to be effective\" in increasing social mobility and risks increased social segregation"
      },
      {
        "tier": "projected",
        "claim": "Critics including the Children's Rights Alliance for England warn removing the cap would entrench segregation and undermine community cohesion.",
        "evidence_id": "E28",
        "quote": "removing the cap would entrench segregation and undermine community cohesion"
      },
